    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0778" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg678"/>

                <head>No. 428.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1880-01-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 16, 1880</date>. (Received
                        February 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1050.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I have the honor to inclose for
                    your information two copies of the official report<anchor n="*" xml:id="d428-f1"
                    /> of the commissioner of the imperial mint of Japan for the year ending June
                    30, 1879.</p>
                <p>It is to be noted that the whole amount of gold received at the min for the year
                    was but 48,853.81 ounces troy, and that the amount of silver <pb facs="0779"
                        n="679" xml:id="pg679"/> imported into the mint for the year was
                    1,638,082.97 ounces troy (pages 3 &amp; 4).</p>
                <p>The entire coinage at the mint from the commencement thereof up to the 30th of
                    June, 1879, amounted in value to 86,219,050.57 yen, of which amount 52,562,739
                    yen were gold.</p>
                <p>On the 30th of June last the amount of gold, silver, and copper bullion and coin
                    held by the mint was as follows: gold, 3,829.28 ounces; silver, 351,587.20
                    ounces; copper, 5,342,997.86 ounces.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
